# How git should handle the file types in this repository.
#
# Only the binaries are declared. Text is deliberately left alone: this machine
# runs core.autocrlf=true, every text file is stored LF and checked out CRLF,
# and that has worked since the beginning. Adding `* text=auto` would
# re-normalise the whole tree and produce a diff touching every file for no
# behavioural gain — a large, unreviewable change to fix nothing.

# `binary` is git's macro for `-text -diff`: never translate line endings, and
# never try to produce a textual diff.
#
# Git's own content detection has been getting these right on its own, which is
# why nothing has broken. This makes it a rule rather than a lucky guess. The
# case it guards against is a PNG whose leading bytes happen to look textual to
# the heuristic: the signature is 89 50 4E 47 0D 0A 1A 0A, and those 0D 0A bytes
# are exactly what an end-of-line filter rewrites. A share card that has had its
# own signature edited is not a corrupted image, it is not an image at all, and
# it fails in somebody else's link preview rather than here.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
# A woff2 is a compressed container and git's heuristic has never mistaken one
# for text, but the argument above about the PNG signature applies word for
# word: the format is entirely binary, an end-of-line filter rewriting a byte
# inside it produces a file that is not a font, and it fails on somebody
# else's machine rather than here.
*.woff2 binary
